  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev700.html",
  "prefLabel": "Rev 707.03 Use of United States Currency",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 707.03 Use of United States Currency.\n\n(a) The tax shall be calculated and imposed on the consumer using the US dollar as the appropriate currency.\n\n(b) Operators shall remit all taxes collected to the department using the US dollar as the basis for calculating their liability.\n\n(c) Operators shall not remit any foreign currency to the department in payment of their meals and rentals liability for tax, interest, or penalties.\n\nSource. #5912, eff 10-14-94; ss by #6750, eff 5-19-98; ss by #8653, eff 6-9-06; ss by #10714, eff 11-7-14 (from Rev 705.03); ss by #14105, eff 10-29-24, EXPIRES: 10-29-34",
